<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage (Coturnix japonica (Japanese quail), Holocene extant, 0 Ma)",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 22.42 µm on Holocene Coturnix japonica plumage faithfully reproduces Coturnix japonica (Japanese quail), Holocene extant, 0 Ma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coturnix japonica (Japanese quail), Holocene extant, 0 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Coturnix japonica (Japanese quail), Holocene extant, 0 Ma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Schnakenberg rates are fitted Shh/Bmp2 biochemical constants.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a geological shift from a named fossil chronospecies. The series is one Holocene node at 0 Ma.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the growth-moment RMSE has been tuned to zero. A parabolic peak fit was tested and rejected because the supercritical sigma peak is not the onset k_c.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du sweep of the linear-regime growth wavelength (Pearson r = 0.9997, RMSE = 6.52 µm) and a nominal dispersion-curve Pearson r = 0.993.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion ablation drawn on the same color scale as the patterned field, so a flat control stays flat.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Full plumage mask and a flank-only ROI on the Yehliu photograph. The figure labels linear 22.42 µm and saturated FFT 33.6 µm as different lengths.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters (a, b, Du, Dv) = (0.07, 0.93, 0.035, 1.85) with the length unit fixed so the onset lambda_c = 2.242e-5 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Harris et al. 2005: Shh self-activates and induces Bmp2; Bmp2 represses Shh on the feather epithelium.",
        "reported_in_source: Haupaix et al. 2018 and Inaba & Chuong 2020: Japanese quail has a somite-scale macro pattern and a within-feather micro pattern.",
        "reported_in_source: Prum & Williamson 2002: within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as follicular reaction-diffusion.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Yehliu portrait has no micron scale bar. GIF pixels are a display envelope. 22.42 µm is the onset law; 33.6 µm is the saturated spot spacing." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/coturnix_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Coturnix japonica (Japanese quail), Holocene extant, 0 Ma; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: the kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Prum & Williamson 2002: within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as follicular reaction-diffusion. | Harris et al. 2005: Shh self-activates and induces Bmp2; Bmp2 represses Shh on the feather epithelium. | Haupaix et al. 2018 and Inaba & Chuong 2020: Japanese quail has a somite-scale macro pattern and a within-feather micro pattern.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot parameters (a, b, Du, Dv) = (0.07, 0.93, 0.035, 1.85) with the length unit fixed so the onset lambda_c = 2.242e-5 m. | Du sweep of the linear-regime growth wavelength (Pearson r = 0.9997, RMSE = 6.52 µm) and a nominal dispersion-curve Pearson r = 0.993. | Equal-diffusion ablation drawn on the same color scale as the patterned field, so a flat control stays flat. | Full plumage mask and a flank-only ROI on the Yehliu photograph. The figure labels linear 22.42 µm and saturated FFT 33.6 µm as different lengths.; transfer_boundary: The Yehliu portrait has no micron scale bar. GIF pixels are a display envelope. 22.42 µm is the onset law; 33.6 µm is the saturated spot spacing.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Schnakenberg rates are fitted Shh/Bmp2 biochemical constants. | Does not claim a geological shift from a named fossil chronospecies. The series is one Holocene node at 0 Ma. | Does not claim the growth-moment RMSE has been tuned to zero. A parabolic peak fit was tested and rejected because the supercritical sigma peak is not the onset k_c.]; phenomenon_size: 2.0 mm (0.002 m, log10=-2.699 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 2.0 mm to 2.0 mm): 2.0 mm:avian-plumage-somite-stripes" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0500781102>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2001.1896>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aar4777>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fcell.2020.00620> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coturnix-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
